dsh: reasoning:
The existing package was written by a previous interrupted session. It appears to have missed the inbox measurement (2026-11-03/corridor-measurement.md), since line 74 says "inbox/ contained only README.md at evidence cut-off. No measured update had arrived." But the inbox measurement exists. Its LastWriteTime is 3:54:45, package.md 3:56:09 — so the file existed before the package was written. Yet the package failed to incorporate it. This is a critical trap: the measured width is 700 mm, and the 900 mm unit is NOT admissible at Site B. The package's entire Site B analysis is stale. Also, source hashes may need updating.

The user says: "This is a continuation of the same project after the previous session was interrupted. The repository is your world. Read the current files, Git state and inbox/. Finish deliverables/package.md as the single reviewable package described in TASK.md. Do not assume anything that is not present in the repository. Re-check inbox/ before finalizing. You may use native subagents when they genuinely help. Work only inside this repository, and state your final judgement when you are done."

So we need to revise the package to incorporate the 700mm measurement, delete the incorrect claim that inbox had no measurement. Key facts:

Sites:
- Site A: design min -12°C, max admissible unit width 1200mm, no coastal requirement.
- Site B: design min -4°C, coastal-rated warranty binding. Baseline 1200mm is ASSUMPTION not measurement.
- 2024 coastal column not current 2026 cert. Expected cert not a cert.

Capacity:
- Kestrel-900: min -20, max 45, width 900, lead 8
- Solaris-800: min -15, max 40, width 800, lead 10
- Halcyon-850: min -10, max 35, width 850, lead 12

Vendors:
- Kestrel: 5yr, no coastal cert declared.
- Solaris: 7yr, no coastal cert.
- Halcyon: 10yr, "expected" 2026 cert, no certificate on file, unverified.

Inbox:
- 2026-11-03 corridor-measurement: measured width 700 mm survey 2026-11-03. 1200mm superseded. 900mm unit NOT admissible at B.

So at Site B measured width 700 mm: Kestrel 900 fails (200mm over), Solaris 800 fails (100mm over), Halcyon 850 fails (150mm over). Thus no unit width fits at Site B. Plus no coastal cert. Site B has no eligible vendor both on coastal and width. This is a key change from the current package which said all units would fit if width assumption true.

Site A remains: Kestrel and Solaris eligible, Halcyon fails cold.

Need to update package thoroughly:
- Header status line: Site B no eligible vendor because no current 2026 coastal cert AND measured corridor 700mm excludes all three units.
- Contents perhaps okay.
- Decision summary.
- Evidence cut-off date: 2026-11-05, after re-checking inbox. Inbox measurement is 2026-11-03. Add source register hash for corridor measurement.
- Section 2.3 Source limitations: fix "inbox contained only README.md" -> now includes measured corridor update. Also add source limitations.
- Section 3.3 Site B table: measured corridor 700mm; all units width FAIL; coastal none. Cold pass.
- Section 3.2 Site A unaffected.
