- Section 6 schedule: Site B blocked by width + certificate; note measured 700mm means none of the current units fit, so Site B needs narrower unit (new model) or civil works to widen corridor. Critical path. Remove "If Site B width measures below 900 mm..." because now we know 700. Section 6.5 update.
- Section 7 risks: R-03 changed from "assumption" to "measured 700 mm excludes all current units" — risk resolved/transformed. Add civil works / narrower unit risk. Mention inbox measurement. R-12 unverified claim remains. R-02.
- Section 8 integrated decision: G1 Site B 0 of 3 due to width and coastal; Site B hold. Update 8.2, 8.4, 8.5.
- Section 9 conditions: add Site B width remediation: either 700mm corridor widening (civil works) or select unit width <=700mm (none in current table), then certificate. Add survey report already exists (measured 700 mm). The C2 condition should now be a design decision/civil works. C3 certificate. RFQ questions update.
- Section 10 claim ledger: add measured width claim, update "No measured Site B width" missing -> now declared measured 700mm. Update source register hash for inbox/2026-11-03/corridor-measurement.md. Need compute SHA-256. Also revision record update to note re-check and supersession. Add evidence hierarchy.
- There might be inconsistencies e.g. line 8 decision line says "no current 2026 coastal certificate ... and 1200 mm corridor is unmeasured assumption" — needs update.
- Also line 32 "Site width is unmeasured" -> now measured 700.
- Line 74 "inbox contained only README.md" -> fixed.
- Line 92 "At Site B this test cannot be completed because the width is an assumption." -> fixed.
- Line 122-126 Site B table.
